    "body": "The selected learned continuation artifact still has eight complete replies, while five new actual trajectories reach factual tokens and fail. This change authenticates and captures those five failures, all eight genuine factual successes and three separate grammar frames at their saved actual prefixes, then audits full action competition and source provenance.\n\nExactly sixteen production integer-native steps at source `70b2c556b3b52ab5b57c0767b95abf9512825a5f` reproduce the saved decisions. Each request binds row hash, ID, position, actual prefix and winner chain. All captures finish before labels are attached separately. Full base Generate/physical Copy vectors, learned U deltas, every physical occurrence, the pre-U bridge donor and finite factor contributions are retained. Saved-vector controls independently reduce Generate-only and removal of U from Copy alone, retaining U on Generate; each recomputes its own common reference, clipping and aliases. No fit, gradient, serving policy or generated counterfactual is introduced.\n\n**Neither control corrects any of the five factual failures.** Removing Copy-side U preserves all eight factual successes; Generate-only loses all eight. Rows97/156 choose the wrong authored source role. Rows151/392 choose later words from the correct source version. Row245 has a wrong base bridge donor, while U changes its final winner into the expected source at the wrong offset; it remains incorrect. At grammar row399, Generate-only chooses2032 rather than315 and removal of Copy-side U still chooses520. These observations exclude the proposed local U-only/Copy-removal repair, not a geometry family.\n\nThe sealed input-only panel reference `54489a02b0b49fe17efc99c514667bac553628b9dee8eea564a3c49a0bfbf594` supplies expected role/event/record/commit after capture. Its authenticated authoring source uses explicit query/cue and namespace/relation mappings plus latest matching event. The audit joins that exact expected tuple to the measured donor and every winning Copy alias, preserving word/byte provenance. The reference never selects runtime sources. A donor mismatch does not establish that replacing it fixes a reply.\n\nValidation: eight focused example tests, formatting, optimized compilation and exact-source mathematical/adversarial reviews PASS. The independent reader verifies65536 base Generate scores,65536 U scores, all production pools,32 full diagnostic reductions, actual correct-prefix membership and physical alias/source-version provenance. Three actual Rust complete-file seals PASS. The reader does not independently reexecute Context/cue/prefix kernels, inference, tokenization or backward. Two initial wrappers selected an unsupported core CUDA feature and failed before tests/model; corrected checks pass and both receipts are retained. Reader reporting/cohort checks were repaired before the single capture; no capture was repeated.\n\nReport `8f99cc6ad83f5ec6901a4ecae4f6783bf469dbb30a949d177b0e636c796af076`, seal `e698e92c4c4fcd1e743808c0ffe901916cf1716f1ffc048f4848186986a5e458`:20 files/82388813 payload bytes. Runtime HF `04a9b3d32695141d6adc1560b2611c572ae629e3` and complete result HF `710bd601fda1879cc44415a1c0f0bec568aba975` are freshly downloaded/hash verified. Capture supervisor30.146723s/RSS208160KiB; reader27.364766s/RSS98596KiB. Full evidence and costs are tracked in current state and the structured receipt. Cumulative projected allowance476070→490470s preserves prior charges; all work uses the authorized pod and per-lab target.\n\nA justified successor is one bounded adaptation of existing Cue/Prefix coefficient credit for source role and occurrence ordering. It must use the full Generate/Copy/U objective and recompute Generate whenever a base Copy change switches the bridge donor. That learning task is NOT_ADMITTED before this protected delivery is verified. The original eight complete replies remain the behavioral boundary; no new useful conversation, transfer or energy claim follows.\n\nReferences #820.\n",
